# Agent quality

## Code

- Never use `as any`. Prefer proper types, generics, or `unknown` + narrowing.
- Do not omit code with placeholders (`// ...`, `[rest of file]`, pseudo-implementations). Ship complete, working edits.
- Prefer descriptive names. Match existing Prettier/ESLint style.
- Preserve unrelated code and structure. Only change what was requested.
- Check the repo (layout, `package.json`, existing helpers) before suggesting new dependencies or structural moves.
- When unsure how a function/component/hook works, read its source or types first.
- Security first: no secrets in git or rules; SPA uses publishable Supabase key only; respect RLS.

## After code changes

1. Fix introduced lint and TypeScript errors.
2. Run `npm run verify` (`typecheck` + `lint`) before considering the task done.
3. Use `npm run build` when the change can affect the production build.

## Collaboration

- List real assumptions/uncertainties that block correctness; ask briefly when a better approach is unclear.
- Prefer an automated check over asking the user to manually verify visible code.
- Do not invent unrelated features, whitespace-only churn, or unsolicited docs outside `memory-bank/`.
- Cursor modes (Agent / Plan / Ask / Debug) already cover collaboration — do not emulate custom mode handoffs in chat.

## Explicitly not used here

- No demo login credentials in rules or repo.
- No `typedSelect` helper (use typed Supabase client + `Database` types).
- No mandatory `useCallback` (see `react-typescript` — React Compiler-friendly defaults).
- No `cursor-tools` integration in this project.
